Release remains blocked for production publication, not because the Lab attack chain is incomplete.

Current automated Lab CI:
- Builds the genuine PHP/Markdown/Chromium target.
- Runs an independent HTTP-only attacker on an internal Docker network.
- Proves stored Markdown XSS in target-local Chromium.
- Reads the private Web Flag through the real loopback-only PHP file reader and path traversal.
- Repeats the full path on two clean instances with different random Flags and checks exact values.
- Checks the default target Flag seed matches the learner Challenge answer.

Separate production gates remain outside this Lab CI:
- Worker lifecycle/network/resource integration.
- Web backend Challenge grading and production Flag configuration.

Do not require a manual learner walkthrough for the Lab E2E gate. Do not expose the vulnerable target to the public Internet.
